        <p>NV-ARRINGTON BLUE COAT CHARITY SCHOOL. NOTICE IS REREBY GIVEN, that the Trustees It the above School will, at their next Quarterly ceeAin tg. on the 17th day of April next, pro- VA lc elect four Children (four Boys) to new existing in the Institution. No nis behlf Z-T'uout,ldate 'Will be eligible unless an application on (forms of which may be obtained in ha Clerkat his Office. 3, Winwick-street, shall have bee • n made to the Clerk to the Trustees ing. fou a least rteen days previous to the day of Meet- th!nir efilecrstting Children, the Trustees make Orphans choice. Those deprived of one parent come next in consideration, and after them the children of parents who have the greatest number and the slenderest means. -Dated this 15th day of March. 1916. HENRY GREENALL, Clerk to the Trustees. ATTESTED MARRIED MEN I</p>
