      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-03-18_WidnesExaminer_art0177" n="art0177">
        <head>PLAY Tilt ME.</head>
        <p>PLAY Tilt ME.</p>
        <p>Mr. Locker And Difference Between Germans And British.</p>
        <p>Ur. Thomas Locker has been appointed President of the Warrington Cricket and Bowling Club, as brielly reported in last week's "Examiner."</p>
        <p>Mr. Locker, in acknowledging the 'honour, Promised to do all he could to maintain the Prestige that had been gained for the'club by the many men—the best and foremost in War- rington—who had occupied the chair before aim- In the course of years the club had developed an important social side, its cricket ground, bowling greens and tennis courts pro- viding a meeting place, on terms of equality, for men and women of diverse political faith, iseligious creed and social rank. On our ground," be proceeded, "amidst Pleasant surroundings we can forget religious differences, political divisions, and social cleavages, and be absolutely united in our Physical, mental, and social relaxation. The Only condition I take it for admission to our club is that the applicant shall be a 'sport,' that he shall play the game.' It matters not to us whether a man be the bluest of Tories or the reddest of Radicals, whether he be orthodox or 'heterodox, Whether he be a millionaire or a pauper; be it DOES matter Whether he is prepared under all circumstances to play cricket (Hear, hear.) And, if I may sal' so, I think that here lies the fundamental difference between ourselves as a people and our national foes. Our national faults no doubt are many, but we, and especially our brave lads at the Front and on the seas, always play the game, 'play cricket.' (Hear, hear.) The Germans don't understand what the mental and moral spirit is that lies behind the scorn and hatred we feel for treachery, and cruelty, and striving ,to win by every foul means, foul apparently in preference to fair, and because they don't know what playing cricket is they drop bombs on innocent women and children, they torpedo helpless and de- fenceless passenger ships, and they fill the World with hellish lies. I sincerely hope that before my year of office shall have expired they will have learnt by bitter experience that the ultimate penalty of not playing the game is inevitable—defeat and destruction, and, What is perhaps worse, the universal contempt of all decent people for all time. (Applause.)</p>
