      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-03-18_WidnesExaminer_art0213" n="art0213">
        <p>Shops, Businesses, Se.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-03-18_WidnesExaminer_art0214" n="art0214">
        <head>Tea and Song at Golborne Street.</head>
        <p>Tea and Song at Golborne Street.</p>
        <p>On Thursday evening a very enjoyable time was spent by a good assembly in connection with a. cake and apron stall arranged by two classes of lady workers concerned with the forthcoming sale bf work. Tea was partaken of, after which a concert was given. An excellent programme had been arranged, Mr. E. Balmford rendering several delightful 'cello solos. Private Balm- ford also contributed, as did Miss Olive Bairn- ford, Miss G. Bowers, Mrs. Littlewood and Miss Ivy Owen.</p>
      </div>
      <div type="article" xml:id="PressMint-GB_1916-03-18_WidnesExaminer_art0215" n="art0215">
        <gap reason="ocrQuality" quantity="1" unit="words">
          <desc>skipped/gap: fewer than 20 non-control characters after cleanup</desc>
        </gap>
      </div>
