        <p>Legal Notices. RE MARY POLDING, Deceased.—Pursuant to the Act of Parliament of the 22nd and 23rd Viet., c. 35, NOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN that all Creditors and other persons having any debts, claims or dethands a-ainst the estate of Mary 'Polding, late of Grayshott, Elm Tree-road, Lymm, in the County of Chester, Spinster, deceased, who died on the 24th day-of February, 1916, are hereby required to send in the particulars of their debts, claims or demands to Me, the undersigned, the Solicitor for the Executors, on or before the 17th day of April, 1916, after which date the said Executors will proceed to distribute the assets ,of the said deceased amongst the pergons entitled thereto, having regard only to the claims and de- mands of which they shall then have had notice: and 'they will not' be liable for the assets of the said deceased, or any part thereof, so distribufed to any Person or persons of whose debts, clanns or de- mands they shall not then have had notice. Dated this 15th day of March, 1916: T. L. C. PRESTON. 36, Spring Gardens, Manchester, Solicitor for the said Executors.</p>
