        <p>CI.IIICIiEN REARING.—Mr. Wm. Coombes, kJ of the " Pleck Gate Poultry Farm," winner of the Ist Prize in the Blackburn and District Lay- ing Competition for four months ending the 4th February, 1916, writes:— "I have always made a practice of using the best food, which I am convineed is the cheapest in the end. My nen of four Buff Orpington Pullets, which laid 316 EGGS in the above competition were reared from the shell on ENTWISTLE BROS.' DRY CHICK FOOD AND CHICKEN MEAL, which I consider to be the best and most reliable on the market. The Pen of Birds from which the winners were bred were also fed on this firm's various lines, and I have no hesitation in recommending them to others." You can get it from your Grocer or Corn Dealer in 341 b. and 71b. bags. Ask for it to-day. Sole manu- facturers: ENTWISTLE BROS., River-st., Bolton. Agents: Carter &amp; Son, Ltd. Barlow &amp; Sons, Warrington: T. Gregory, Earleslown.</p>
